  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Swept Driveway",
    "overview": "The page reads like a job just finished: clean, ordered, nothing left lying around. It is Ellie's house calm band style. Full-bleed bands alternate between a cool off-white paper and two indigos taken from the logo, so every new section is obvious at a glance on a phone. One warm gold carries every action. The only photograph in the hero is the client's own washed driveway, held under an indigo veil so white type sits on it without effort.\n\nDensity is low and generous: one idea per band, a 20px phone gutter, 64px of band padding on phones and 96px from tablet width. Shapes are soft and borderless (24px cards, full pills, tinted fields), depth comes from band colour and translucent white glass, not from shadows. Motion is small and earned: the hero headline bounces in letter by letter once, things below the first screen rise 12px as they arrive, each before/after slider sweeps once to show it moves, and a single gold contact circle floats in after the hero.\n\nThe earlier \"fogged dusk window\" world (mist, painted frames, canvas fog, water seams) is gone and is not part of this system.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Alternating full-bleed bands: paper, navy, paper, deep indigo with a faint 135deg line texture.",
      "One warm accent, gold, used as a fill; gold text only on dark bands, a darker gold-ink on light.",
      "Cal Sans for every heading and every tappable label; the system stack for running text at 16/1.7.",
      "Soft borderless shapes on a fixed radius ladder (24 / 20 / 18 / 16 / 10 / 8 / pill).",
      "Flat surfaces; only the slider knob and the floating circle cast a shadow.",
      "Real photography only: the client's driveway and three real before/after pairs."
    ],
